From cbb18b2e7ceab0c80248e607bf178f1327d11df8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:47:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 049/146] hydra: list Cycles GPU before Cycles CPU in the
 engine menu

Both entries already existed, but in Houdini's order for Karma - CPU on top.
Karma has its reasons (its XPU is still young), we do not: the OptiX path is
the one Cycles has been using for years, and it is the one every user coming
from Blender thinks they are choosing.

Measured on an RTX 3090, same scene, husk:

    fixed cost alone (1 sample)      CPU 5.4 s   GPU 3.6 s
    1024 samples at 960x720          CPU 9.1 s   GPU 4.7 s

That is about four times the tracing throughput, and a shorter startup on top.
Choosing "Cycles CPU" unintentionally, because it was listed first, therefore
silently cost all that.

For reference, on the same scene Karma starts in 6.9 s: husk's fixed cost is
not ours, it is the host's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/resources/UsdRenderers.json | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/hydra/resources/UsdRenderers.json b/src/hydra/resources/UsdRenderers.json
index 7633f371..33dd2cc4 100644
--- a/src/hydra/resources/UsdRenderers.json
+++ b/src/hydra/resources/UsdRenderers.json
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
     "HdCyclesPlugin" : {
         "valid" : true,
         "menulabel" : "Cycles CPU",
-        "menupriority" : 45,
+        "menupriority" : 44,
         "defaultpurposes" : [ "render" ],
         "drawmodesupport" : false,
         "needsdepth" : false,
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
     "HdCyclesPluginGPU" : {
         "valid" : true,
         "menulabel" : "Cycles GPU",
-        "menupriority" : 44,
+        "menupriority" : 45,
         "defaultpurposes" : [ "render" ],
         "drawmodesupport" : false,
         "needsdepth" : false,
